{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shapeWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.shapeWitness","kind":"instance","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L129-L135","doc":"**Non-vacuity — the shape-witness.** `τ = 5/2`, `θ = 2`: `2² − (5/2)·2 + 1 = 4 − 5 + 1 = 0`, so `θ = 2`\nis a genuine root of the characteristic polynomial (its partner is `θ⁻¹ = 1/2`, and `2 + 1/2 = 5/2 = τ`).\nThis witnesses the *shape* of the class — it is **not** a claim that the actual Seifert `M` has trace\n`5/2` (`τ ≈ 2.6424` is never fitted; the geometric identification is the open owner-gated object). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.framing_reconstructs_monodromy_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.framing_reconstructs_monodromy_trace","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L117-L127","doc":"**Bridge to the actual Gauss–Manin monodromy trace.** For any `BringWPlaneMonodromy` instance `mon`\n(carrying the unimodular Seifert operator `M`, `tr M = τ`), a `StokesMonodromyFraming` at `τ = tr M`\nreconstructs that trace from its twist pair: `θ + θ⁻¹ = tr M`. This states the fibre→observable passage\nin monodromy language against the corpus's actual `M` — the categorical \"`continuation = M acts`\",\nmodulo the open geometric identification `mon.is_seifert_gauss_manin`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_mul_inv_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_mul_inv_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L108-L113","doc":"**The eigenvalue product is `1`** (unimodularity at the eigenvalue level): `θ · θ⁻¹ = 1`. The\nconstant term `1` of the characteristic polynomial is `det M = 1` — the symplectic structure of `H¹(E)`\nread off the roots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_add_inv_eq_tau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_add_inv_eq_tau","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L98-L106","doc":"**The fibre/observable twist pair reconstructs the monodromy trace: `θ + θ⁻¹ = τ`.** Sum of the two\neigenvalues `θ, θ⁻¹` equals `tr M = τ`. From `eigen` + `θ ≠ 0`. This is the genuine, sorry-free bridge:\nthe twist pair `(θ_λ, θ_{λ'}) = (θ, θ⁻¹)` reconstructs the `BringWPlaneMonodromy` trace scalar `τ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_inv_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_inv_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L86-L96","doc":"**The other monodromy eigenvalue is `θ⁻¹`** — `θ⁻¹` solves the *same* characteristic polynomial.\nMultiply `eigen` by `θ⁻²` and use `θ ≠ 0`: the two roots of the unimodular `x² − τx + 1` are `θ, θ⁻¹`\n(product `= 1`). This is the Riemann–Hilbert incarnation of the transpose / chirality law\n`θ_{λ'} = θ_λ⁻¹` (`KeystoneModularTwist.theta_conjugate`, #3662): **the transpose `λ ↦ λ'` supplies the\nsecond monodromy eigenvalue.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L78-L84","doc":"**The twist eigenvalue is nonzero.** From `eigen`: if `θ = 0` the characteristic relation collapses\nto `1 = 0`. (Unimodularity forbids a zero eigenvalue — the eigenvalue product is the constant term `1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.eigen","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L72-L72","doc":"**CONTENT.** `θ` solves the unimodular monodromy's characteristic polynomial\n`x² − τ·x + 1 = 0` (`τ = tr M`) — i.e. `θ` is a monodromy eigenvalue. This is the Cayley–Hamilton\nresidue of `unimodular_two_recurrence`, evaluated on the eigenvalue `θ` rather than the operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.theta","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The `λ`-graded ribbon twist eigenvalue `θ_λ` carried on this block (the framing datum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.StokesMonodromyFraming","kind":"class","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowStokesMonodromy.lean#L56-L72","doc":"**The fibre↔observable passage as a Stokes / Gauss–Manin monodromy action (§3b class).**\n\nCONTENT: the ribbon twist `θ_λ` — the framing that distinguishes the fibre value (`‖q‖=1`) from the\nobservable value (`q₀>1`) — is an **eigenvalue** of the unimodular monodromy `M`, i.e. it satisfies `M`'s\ncharacteristic (Cayley–Hamilton) relation `x² − (tr M)·x + 1 = 0` with `τ = tr M`. This is the\nRiemann–Hilbert statement that \"continuation to `q₀`\" *is* \"apply the monodromy\", not an analytic limit.\n\nThe single field `eigen` carries the residue as a parameter-quantified polynomial equation in the shape\nof the characteristic relation of `unimodular_two_recurrence` — genuine content, discharged for a\nconcrete shape-witness but **open** for the actual Seifert `M` (`BringWPlaneMonodromy`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}